# MASTER BUILD PROMPT — PLUSONE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, product designer, UX researcher, database architect, and quality assurance engineer.

Build a complete, production-oriented, responsive social discovery web application called **PlusOne.**

Do not create only a landing page, static prototype, design mockup, or disconnected frontend. Build a functional end-to-end application with real authentication, persistent database storage, backend logic, user interactions, security rules, and complete user journeys.

## 1. Product concept

Product name: PlusOne.

Primary tagline: Find your people. Go somewhere.

Secondary tagline: Good plans. Better company.

Brand philosophy: Life is better with a PlusOne.

PlusOne is an activity-first social discovery platform that helps people find others to participate in real-world activities.

Many people want to visit museums, attend events, explore cities, go hiking, visit cafes, watch movies, or try new experiences but postpone their plans because they have nobody to accompany them.

PlusOne solves this problem by allowing people to create activities, discover nearby plans, request to join small groups, communicate with approved participants, and meet in real life.

The central product insight is:

"Don't match people based on who they are. Match them based on what they want to do."

This is not a dating application. Do not include romantic matching, profile swiping, attractiveness ratings, or dating terminology.

The product should encourage meaningful offline interactions instead of endless online engagement.

