## 12. Join request workflow

Implement a real, database-backed request and approval system.

When a user clicks "Request to join":

- Open a confirmation modal.
- Allow an optional introductory message.
- Create a join request in Firestore.
- Notify the activity host.
- Change the button to "Request pending."
- Prevent duplicate active requests.
- Allow the user to withdraw a pending request.

The host must be able to:

- View incoming requests.
- View relevant public profile information.
- Approve a request.
- Decline a request.
- View approved participants.
- Remove a participant when necessary.

When approved:

- Update the request status.
- Update the activity's approved participant count.
- Add the activity to the user's My Plans.
- Notify the user.
- Grant access to the activity group chat and meeting instructions.

Use a secure server-side transaction for approval and capacity updates.

Prevent race conditions and overbooking when multiple requests are approved simultaneously.

The host cannot request to join their own activity.

Users cannot join cancelled, completed, expired, or full activities.

