## 23. Security and privacy

Generate complete Firestore and Cloud Storage security rules.

Follow least-privilege access.

Requirements:

- Users can edit only their own profile.
- Private profile data is accessible only to its owner and authorized backend services.
- Public activities can be discovered without exposing private participant information.
- Only hosts can manage their own activities.
- Only authorized hosts can approve requests.
- Users can access their own requests.
- Hosts can access requests for their activities.
- Only approved participants and hosts can access private activity details and group chat.
- Notifications are readable only by their intended recipient.
- Administrative privileges must be assigned securely on the server.
- Users cannot grant themselves administrator access.
- Reports must not be publicly readable.
- Validate file types and upload sizes.
- Implement rate limiting and abuse prevention where appropriate.
- Sanitize user-generated content.
- Prevent unauthorized database writes.

Never deploy with unrestricted test-mode Firestore rules.

